 and justice ginsburg were friends and  and marty  ginsberg justice ginsburg's late husband  uh was also  you know they they all gathered together  often and  they uh and marty was a great cook and  uh  my dad liked to eat so i think that that  helped the friendship along too  well one thing that uh is it's  refreshing but it really shouldn't be  chris and you touched on it  this idea that politics or what you do  for a living has to define all your  relationships and if there's one thing  that i've  really hated about the last couple of  years and that's really the last 10  years in washington  is how that has infected  everything from entertainment industry  to sports  to i mean we can't get away from  politics in these  pitched ideological battles and that  really shouldn't be everything about a  relationship  any relationship frankly friendships  family and  it's so i guess um it's like kind of a  bygone  era it feels like now but maybe that's  just washington dc yeah i mean  yeah i i i think a lot of us have  friends who disagree with us  and we we're we're friends for other  reasons and  maybe things maybe that is becoming more  and more difficult but i think one of  the reasons people  people uh really kind of look up to the  friendship that they had  was because they not not just because it  seems rare but because deep down they  also know it's possible  and and they have approximate  friendships but but i want to i want to  share a story that  that i i only heard recently uh judge  jeff sutton of the sixth circuit clerked  for my father  and and was visiting him uh shortly  before i think shortly before my father  passed away and it was justice  ginsburg's birthday  and uh my dad had two dozen roses  to give to justice ginsburg so he said  uh he said sorry jeff i got to go i got  to bring this down to ruth's office  and and jeff said two dozen roses why  are you  uh he was he was teasing my dad saying  what's the point of giving her two dozen  roses  what what do you get out of this what is  the last time she sided with you in a  5-4 decision  and and judge sutton was was kind of  kidding around but my dad took it  seriously and said  jeff some things are more important than  votes  and i think that really captures the  significance of their friendship and  kind of uh  why it should be so significant to us  too  chris it was important to hear from you  tonight thank you so much for joining us  we really appreciate it  thanks for having me
 

